# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command regs
usage 1   regs                          CPU + video (+ APU/coprocessor) registers
usage 2   regs <cpu>                    just one processor's registers - `cpus` lists them
usage 3   (to WRITE a register, see `setreg` - kept separate so `regs` stays read-only)

case registers
target fake
covers 1-3
$ regs
out 233
GOLDEN CPU registers:
  PC   = 0x8003
  A    = 0x12
  X    = 0x0340
  P    = 0x34
Video registers:
  SCANLINE = 0x70
  MODE     = 0x01
APU registers:
  APU0      = 0xAA
Coprocessor registers:
  R15       = 0x0020
  SFR       = 0x0002
status 0
action none
$ regs cpu
out 109
the main processor registers:
  PC        = 0x8003
  A         = 0x12
  X         = 0x0340
  P         = 0x34
status 0
action none
$ regs gsu
out 75
a graphics coprocessor registers:
  R15       = 0x0020
  SFR       = 0x0002
status 0
action none
$ regs cop
out 61
No debug CPU named 'cop' on this GOLDEN. Available: cpu, gsu.
status 0
action none
$ regs nope
out 62
No debug CPU named 'nope' on this GOLDEN. Available: cpu, gsu.
status 0
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
